[{"id":"VRCE-3-67-1","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":1,"english":"O Mighty armed Rāma of great prowess, formerly my beauty, beyond conception, was known all over the three worlds, like to the beauty of the Sun, the Moon and Indra. I used to frighten everywhere the ascetics living in the forest by turning this my beauty into a terrific form.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.739,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067001","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bab14ac74288184771be62e41901a90bd75cd80e77cb78bad250206d53b6dff","compact":"f3f0fda51638fcb12f622b2343123c09db7dbf96f46fdc21818d17d2c66604e1","nasal":"7960f058adf905d38c72b2d25b4f21e63ec3c2ba13ae3b8b2ed11fb355859749"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-2","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":2,"english":"O Mighty armed Rāma of great prowess, formerly my beauty, beyond conception, was known all over the three worlds, like to the beauty of the Sun, the Moon and Indra. I used to frighten everywhere the ascetics living in the forest by turning this my beauty into a terrific form.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067002","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9d26aca8f2dd1d4e69b02ecbae3118199308e734171545d085f9f60c57d5fe80","compact":"d58b511432efa61d5a4781996b93a0b6055ce7603ff7f6497f6ba87b05698e13","nasal":"d58b511432efa61d5a4781996b93a0b6055ce7603ff7f6497f6ba87b05698e13"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-3","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":3,"english":"Once on a time assuming this terrible shape I assailed and enraged the great ascetic Sthulasira collecting diverse wild fruits. Thereupon he imprecated curses upon me.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067003","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6ce01814dba7767e74a3e19ed1322e39be33e54d1e11a215feeab47ae02e2a72","compact":"45ec4fb5873fb1c13b54e313d361c5ad3fb54b15d2f2fd3f307839cfce57282e","nasal":"45ec4fb5873fb1c13b54e313d361c5ad3fb54b15d2f2fd3f307839cfce57282e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-4","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":4,"english":"Once on a time assuming this terrible shape I assailed and enraged the great ascetic Sthulasira collecting diverse wild fruits. Thereupon he imprecated curses upon me. Do you retain this ghastly shape hated of all mankind. Upon my praying to that angry ascetic for my relief from that curse, he said.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.5,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-2","DUTT-3-71-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067004","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"42039c0c1ac3716eb1bcd0119649cc443224dd06dd49bfc90eb1f63f76800f71","compact":"5ad4e577141910b32bb67a7461b4067438e2588f2c9b2fa79da279cdcf1ecab1","nasal":"5ad4e577141910b32bb67a7461b4067438e2588f2c9b2fa79da279cdcf1ecab1"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-5","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":5,"english":"Do you retain this ghastly shape hated of all mankind. Upon my praying to that angry ascetic for my relief from that curse, he said.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067005","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c585bec09a16bff362a05574fe53a2cc2da1feb9133688982d2a704c9b550d5b","compact":"b588886c4786f7956b3bc8aa552804978e9352911c7fda351b1f202ab61e4cd9","nasal":"08cba9fda7f77de5c1eb69415c4a978ca687494a7e61dbd038d6e31badc1231f"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-6","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":6,"english":"You shall regain your stalwart and beautiful shape when you shall be burnt by Rāma in a dense forest having got your arms dissevered by him.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067006","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3db97fe6df4f00e6c86862b33c097f2394aa3465812701a5754193bc958594dd","compact":"61f16b73c5657b88b1571d8e4ff4c42fcdec1f57033c70eb6a260d7bfb5bbfa5","nasal":"61f16b73c5657b88b1571d8e4ff4c42fcdec1f57033c70eb6a260d7bfb5bbfa5"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-7","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":7,"english":"You shall regain your stalwart and beautiful shape when you shall be burnt by Rāma in a dense forest having got your arms dissevered by him. O Lakşmaņa, know me to be the beautiful son of Danu. Through Indra's curse in the battle field I have been metamorphosed into my present shape. After I had pleased him with hard austerites, the Grand-Father of the celestials conferred on me a long life. And therefore I was inflamed with pride assailed Indra in a conflict, thinking within me, 'I have gained a long life-what can Indra do me?'","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.493,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-4","DUTT-3-71-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067007","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"083f54f7fd63b98a4c5820ec1e2c6a2357788e9b5ee5b7deaf91805d30ba3621","compact":"d7eb9d915a078d52508fedef1c2c0ff8a6ede3b49e3d6cc1d4df8ce1dd8a8865","nasal":"9810ccd053f3245dd21ca9e40d2d35e6a61f5bd7d41785661f82158a0c3c7252"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-8","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":8,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, know me to be the beautiful son of Danu. Through Indra's curse in the battle field I have been metamorphosed into my present shape. After I had pleased him with hard austerites, the Grand-Father of the celestials conferred on me a long life. And therefore I was inflamed with pride assailed Indra in a conflict, thinking within me, 'I have gained a long life-what can Indra do me?'","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.918,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067008","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b82e88d118e43854e60bb2a79bdb8d95618ed1ec4c3d5d55689ccaa5f846ecec","compact":"27d77aff11127f0039a6a3a30d75009bd91eda3b988adf56264e211895bde923","nasal":"27d77aff11127f0039a6a3a30d75009bd91eda3b988adf56264e211895bde923"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-9","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":9,"english":"O Lakşmaņa, know me to be the beautiful son of Danu. Through Indra's curse in the battle field I have been metamorphosed into my present shape. After I had pleased him with hard austerites, the Grand-Father of the celestials conferred on me a long life. And therefore I was inflamed with pride assailed Indra in a conflict, thinking within me, 'I have gained a long life-what can Indra do me?' Thereupon by his thunderbolt, having hundred edges hurled off his hands, my thighs were shattered and my head thrusted into my body.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.412,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-5","DUTT-3-71-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067009","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"048f756eb09386df5d43c5209b23d6e785c120ecc1d9104fc2f5aeccf6624ac8","compact":"0e6d41d9b818c49892abb09eb456a194b5ead1a12308ab717bae3ceca559a571","nasal":"0e6d41d9b818c49892abb09eb456a194b5ead1a12308ab717bae3ceca559a571"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-10","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":10,"english":"Thereupon by his thunderbolt, having hundred edges hurled off his hands, my thighs were shattered and my head thrusted into my body.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.862,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067010","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"76d53534fadad192d6b57267f6fde8b80e1526907c8e5036db970bcf42465b71","compact":"8d98ec7ee1764d39e6ba3b4c273c912fcb53451a9b36a320b05a880364bfe60e","nasal":"8d98ec7ee1764d39e6ba3b4c273c912fcb53451a9b36a320b05a880364bfe60e"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-11","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":11,"english":"Myself praying for the close of my life, he did not despatch me to the abode of Yama. He only said May the words of the Grand Sire prove true.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067011","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2323a9b3310ddbdc02275da74d52fba37449aa4cad816b956690437d58e973de","compact":"00e8f89fdf817ea4ad2adc5d3b6c1901e6671b0ed14cb5829d800fa42ec7610f","nasal":"2f564076671f88da8a321b9a7f7c4b623569fbe42c5abb6a7fe73ee6399da7e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-3-67-12","kanda":3,"kandaId":"aranya","sarga":67,"verse":12,"english":"Where to I replied 'How shall I live long without any food, being smitten by you having a thunderbolt in your hand, and having my head, thighs and mouth crushed down?' Thereat Indra made my hands extending over a Yojana and placed my mouth, having sharpened teeth, on my belly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-3-71-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"3067012","sanskritFile":"Ram03.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"65d7e7ecbac3c7c702272